#* {{quote-book|en|year=1961|author=Eric Partridge|title=The Routledge Dictionary of Historical Slang|passage='''hog''' ([[plural|pl]] '''hog''')... 2. In [[century|C]].18–early 19, [[occasionally|occ]]. a [[sixpence]]: also [[cant|c]]., whence the U.S. sense. [[probably|Prob]]. [[from|ex]] the figure of a hog on a small silver coin.}}
